# BlogScraper Project Standards

- Keep changes small and focused; avoid broad refactors unless requested.
- Prefer clear, plain-English docstrings and comments for non-obvious logic.
- Preserve runtime behavior unless the task explicitly asks for behavior changes.
- Do not hardcode secrets, keys, or connection strings in code or docs.
- Keep Azure service interactions explicit and observable (clear logs and errors).
- Add or update tests when behavior changes.
- Favor readability over cleverness; optimize only where needed.
- Do not use deprecated Python/PHP APIs.
